== BO$chi$EFT approach to ordinary and exotic hadrons
Nonperturbative QCD: two complementary sources of information, with different degrees of freedom at different distances
#v(0.4em)
#align(center, scale(85%, reflow: true, scales-figure))
#v(0.4em)
- #text(fill: blue)[BOEFT] (Braaten, Brambilla, et al.): coupled Schrödinger equations in coordinate space \
  #text(fill: rgb("#FF6600"))[Pro:] direct correspondence to lattice potentials; #text(fill: rgb("#FF6600"))[Con:] no hadronic degrees of freedom
- #text(fill: blue)[BO$chi$EFT]: coupled Lippmann–Schwinger equations in momentum space \
  #text(fill: rgb("#FF6600"))[Pro:] multibody effects and meson exchanges; #text(fill: rgb("#FF6600"))[Con:] link to short range nontrivial
#v(0.4em)
#align(center, text(fill: red)[*Hope: merge both into one systematically improvable framework*])

