== Coupling bottomonia to $B macron(B)^*$
#grid(
  columns: (auto, 1fr),
  column-gutter: 1.5em,
  align: horizon,
  scale(120%, reflow: true, transition-diagram()),
  [
    - $macron(b)$ and $b$ act as spectators, light $q macron(q)$ pair is created
    - Heavy quarks carry most of the momentum, $p$ enters the $macron(b)b$ wave function
    $
      chevron.l B macron(B)^*(""^3S_1) | hat(g) | [macron(b)b]_1(n P) chevron.r = g psi_n (p)
    $
  ],
)
#v(0.5em)
$
  V_S^((macron(b)b) + "CT")(p', p) = g^2 / (4pi) sum_(n = 1)^N (psi_n (p') psi_n^* (p)) / (M - M_n^((macron(b)b))) + C(N), quad
  psi_n (p) = 4pi integral_0^infinity r^2 dif r thin j_0(p r) R_(1 n)(r)
$
#v(0.3em)
#text(fill: blue)[Channels]: $macron(b)b$ couples only to the $S$ wave, but OME couples $S$ and $D$ waves with $J^(P C) = 1^(++)$
$
  "2-body channels:" quad {B macron(B)^*(""^3S_1), B macron(B)^*(""^3D_1), B^* macron(B)^* (""^5D_1)} \
  "3-body intermediate states:" quad {B macron(B) phi.alt, B^* macron(B)^* phi.alt, B macron(B)^* phi.alt, macron(B)^* B phi.alt}, quad phi.alt = pi, eta
$

