== Born-Oppenheimer symmetries
Static $b$ and $macron(b)$ define an axis $hat(bold(r))$, giving quantum numbers labelled by #text(fill: red)[$Lambda_eta^sigma$]
#v(0.5em)
#align(center, scale(95%, reflow: true, bo-figure()))
#v(0.5em)
Heavy-quark limit: light-degree-of-freedom energies at fixed $r$ $->$ static BO potentials $V_(Lambda_eta^sigma)(r)$
#v(0.3em)
$S$-wave meson pairs: $j_ell^(P C)$, $s_(macron(b)b)^(P C) in {0^(-+), 1^(--)}$, only one combination gives $1^(++)$:
$
  1_ell^(--) times.o 1_(macron(b)b)^(--) = 0^(++) plus.o #text(fill: red)[$1^(++)$] plus.o 2^(++), quad
  lambda_ell = 0 -> #text(fill: red)[$Sigma_g^(+')$], quad lambda_ell = plus.minus 1 -> #text(fill: red)[$Pi_g$]
$

